    <item>
      <title>GitHub Copilot moves into Xcode's built-in coding assistant and JetBrains Air, landing inside two rival agent surfaces in one week</title>
      <link>https://github.blog/changelog/2026-11-04-github-copilot-is-now-available-in-xcodes-coding-assistant/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://github.blog/changelog/2026-11-04-github-copilot-is-now-available-in-xcodes-coding-assistant/</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 05:00:00 -0800</pubDate>
      <category>AI &amp; Agents</category>
      <description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://github.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/694394305-f9d288c4-2862-48ff-aadf-b307e5ead674.png" alt="GitHub Copilot in Xcode" style="max-width:100%"/></p>
<p><b>Public preview in Xcode 27.3 beta on macOS Tahoe 26.6+, set up under Xcode &gt; Settings &gt; Intelligence, working with every Copilot plan; a day earlier Copilot became an agent in JetBrains Air via the Agent Client Protocol - more evidence ACP is becoming the standard socket for coding agents, the way LSP did for language tooling.</b></p>
<p>Sources: <a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2026-11-04-github-copilot-is-now-available-in-xcodes-coding-assistant/">GitHub Changelog (Xcode)</a> &middot; <a href="https://javarubberduck.com/ai/news-2026-11-08-dev-tools/">JavaRubberDuck digest</a></p>
<p>Feedback: <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=Digest%2011/8%3A%20loved%20%22GitHub%20Copilot%20moves%20into%20Xcode%27s%20built...%22">Loved it</a> &middot; <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=Digest%2011/8%3A%20meh%20on%20%22GitHub%20Copilot%20moves%20into%20Xcode%27s%20built...%22">Meh</a> &middot; <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=Digest%2011/8%3A%20less%20like%20%22GitHub%20Copilot%20moves%20into%20Xcode%27s%20built...%22">Less of this</a> &middot; <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=https%3A//github.blog/changelog/2026-11-04-github-copilot-is-now-available-in-xcodes-coding-assistant/%0A">Chat about it</a></p>]]></description>
      <media:content url="https://github.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/694394305-f9d288c4-2862-48ff-aadf-b307e5ead674.png" medium="image"/>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Codex CLI 0.167.0 adds 'codex agents', a command center listing running and finished agent tasks with unread results marked</title>
      <link>https://github.com/openai/codex/releases/tag/rust-v0.167.0</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://github.com/openai/codex/releases/tag/rust-v0.167.0</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 04:30:00 -0800</pubDate>
      <category>AI &amp; Agents</category>
      <description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://opengraph.githubassets.com/7523025ed8317d6dba3b8f2424edd66ab8b0679c6b4ef53b464c771e106c2697/openai/codex/releases/tag/rust-v0.167.0" alt="Codex CLI 0.167.0 release" style="max-width:100%"/></p>
<p><b>OpenAI's Nov. 6 release also switches between connected backends without losing drafts, previews local image attachments while composing, and adds a gcp_setup_wizard that configures Google Cloud Vertex AI with Application Default Credentials.</b></p>
